  "published": "2026-05-10T20:44:04.47Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.2.0:\n- Add IRequestPreProcessor<TRequest> and IRequestPostProcessor<TRequest, TResponse> (MediatR-compatible). Multiple processors per request type are supported and execute in registration order; post-processors are skipped when the handler or any preceding step throws.\n- Add explicit registration via cfg.AddRequestPreProcessor<T>() and cfg.AddRequestPostProcessor<T>(); the wrapper pipeline behaviors are wired automatically when at least one processor is registered.\n- Add cfg.AutoRegisterRequestProcessors flag (default false) for opt-in assembly scanning of processors, mirroring MediatR.\n- AddOpenMediatR no longer throws when no assemblies are configured to scan (matches MediatR); it registers core services and lets you compose the rest explicitly.\n- Fix: AddOpenMediatR is now idempotent across multiple calls for scanned INotificationHandler<>, user pipeline behaviors registered via AddOpenBehavior/AddOpenStreamBehavior, and pre/post-processors (switched to TryAddEnumerable, deduplicating by service+implementation pair).",
